    DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

    HttpServer closes an HTTP/1.x connection after a response with a lingering close: the client reads the response
    and the end of the stream, and whatever it sent that the server did not read is discarded until the client
    closes its side, instead of making the system reset the connection.  The server's DEBUG log reports how much was
    discarded and whether the client closed its side, which the client itself cannot observe.
*/

%modern

%prepend-module-path "${SCRIPT_DIR}/../../../../qlib"
%requires QUnit
%requires Logger
%requires HttpServerUtil
%requires HttpServer

%exec-class HttpServerLingeringCloseTest

